{"id":"u-04751d06-c51d-4716-a485-553875c5235d","src":"community","title":"3-day fighter physique program - Phase 1","author":"B D.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/jHNoBe-3-day-fighter-physique-program-phase-1-1","desc":"This program is designed for athletes, martial artists, and anyone chasing a fighter-style physique — lean, explosive, and resilient.\n\nYou’ll train 3 days per week with a balance of compound strength lifts, explosive movements, and accessory work to build both performance and aesthetics. Unlike bodybuilding splits, this program keeps recovery in mind while still developing the wide-shouldered, lean-waisted look of a fighter. (This is in addition to any martial arts/fighting training you already do or can be used if you want to get in shape before joining a gym - though that shouldn't stop you!).\n\nWhat you should get:\n\nExplosive Strength → deadlifts, squats, and presses programmed for power and athletic carryover.\n\nPhysique Development → targeted accessory work for shoulders, arms, and core to create a balanced, sculpted fighter look.\n\nConditioning → finishers like kettlebell swings, jump rope, and lunges to increase stamina and simulate fight-round intensity.\n\nCore Training → rotational and anti-rotation work to strengthen the midsection for striking, grappling, and overall stability.\n\nTraining Format:\n\n3 days/week (about 65–70 minutes each, including warm-up).\n\nProgressive overload built in — you’ll increase weights, reps, or conditioning volume gradually over 6 weeks.\n\nRPE-based intensity (most lifts at RPE 7–8) to keep you training hard without burning out.\n\nWho it’s for:\n\nbeginner/Intermediate trainees who want to improve athleticism, build muscle, and burn fat while balancing combat sports or conditioning.\n\nPerfect for martial artists, boxers, Krav Maga practitioners, or anyone who wants to look and perform like a fighter.\n\nBy the end of Phase 1, you’ll be stronger, more explosive, and visibly leaner — with the foundation to push into Phase 2 or repeat with heavier loads.","level":["Intermediate","Novice","Beginner"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-08-18T04:33:58.950Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day A – Explosive Strength (Lo","Day B – Push/Pull Upper Power","Day C – Speed, Conditioning"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Inverted Row","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Landmine Oblique Twist","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wpfYRQGYVm4"},{"n":"Kettlebell Swing","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Push Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Jump Squat","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Walking Lunge (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Jump Rope","sets":[{"sec":600,"secHi":900,"rpe":7}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"x":4}]},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Inverted Row","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Landmine Oblique Twist","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note